    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d268-a18">

                <pb facs="0715" n="629" xml:id="pg629"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 18.—Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Soyeshima Tane-omi to
                        Mr. De Long.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Tokei</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="japanese-nengō gregorian"
                            when="1873-08-20">20<hi rendition="#italic">th of the</hi> 8<hi
                                rendition="#italic">th month of</hi> 6<hi rendition="#italic">th
                                year, Meiji</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Your Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge
                    the receipt of your excellency’s dispatch No. 64, dated the 12th instant, in
                    which you advise me that on the 11th you signed the bill of sale of the bark
                    Maria Luz, received from Messrs. Fletcher &amp; Co. the proceeds of her sale,
                    less their account of sales as per their receipt; paid Messrs. Walsh, Hall &amp;
                    Co. their account of expenses of vessel to date according to their receipt, and
                    deposited the balance of ($4,713.28) four thousand seven hundred and thirteen
                    Mexican dollars and twenty-eight cents in the Hong-Kong and Shanghai Banking
                    Corporation of Yokohama, as per copy of certificate to that effect, which
                    receipts and certificate have also come to hand.</p>
                <p>As your action is entirely in accordance with the protocol of June 25, 1873,
                    signed by the envoy extraordinary and minister plenipotentiary of Peru, and the
                    acting minister for foreign affairs of Japan, and with their joint note to you
                    of July 14, 1873, I have only once more to thank your excellency most sincerely
                    in my own name and in the name of my government for the trouble that you have
                    been so kind as to give yourself in this matter.</p>
                <p>With respect and consideration,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>SOYESHIMA TANE OMI.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
